> API and interpretation

The strings are controlled byte fixtures rather than sampled homologous genes. A
high local score alone is not a statistical homology test. No positive score
gives empty rows and zero spans. Complete bordered DP defaults to one million
cells, and optional actual traceback records have their own bound. Integer
overflow is rejected instead of corrupting the recurrence.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Smith and Waterman (1981), Identification of common molecular subsequences|https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-2836(81)90087-5]

